## How it Works

The recommendation model behind this website is a hybrid recommender that combines
collaborative filtering and content-based recommendation to generate recs that are
both similar to the input(s) and also likely to be enjoyed.

Recommendations are made by averaging weighted vector embeddings of each movie
and finding the N closest movies (by cosine similarity) to the resulting average
vector.

Embeddings were created by training a latent-factor model with 50 factors. 
Each movie's metadata was added to the embedding vector as well, by creating a countvectorized soup
of the director (weighted 2x), writers, keywords (weighted 2x), and genres (weighted 7x). 
Lastly, the popularity (vote count on TMDB) and average rating of each movie are
scaled and added to the vector. 

## Data sources

- Ratings: MovieLens latest dataset (~33,000,000 ratings). This dataset
  only has data up to 2023, so recent movies are not included.
- Movie metadata: TMDB

